  "2026-10-16T04:07:33.061Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-10-16: strict complete all-status corpus of 2971 items with zero omissions plus request-specific keyword searches and live open/in_progress reads. No item references GH-1481. Existing foundational owners retain their prior completed scope; this child records the distinct newly reported defect. Kept open and unclaimed while finishing PR 1479."
escape_class: production_defect
body: "## Observed (pm 2026.10.15)\n\n```console\n$ pm list --status open --limit 2 --sort priority --format json | jq -c '.items[0]|keys'\n[\"id\",\"status\",\"title\",\"type\"]\n```\n\nThe result is ordered by `priority`, but the brief projection (`id,status,type,title`) leaves the sort key out. The ordering is visible but the value behind it isn't. An agent that asked for priority order and reads `.priority` gets `null` for every row. Then it either re-runs with `--fields id,priority,...` or misreports priorities. That happened in this session: a backlog survey printed `pnull` for every item.\n\nThe same applies to `--sort updated_at` / `created_at` / `deadline`.\n\n## Proposal\n\nWhen `--sort <field>` is given and `--fields` is not, add the sort field to the brief projection. In TOON that is one extra column. Record it in `projection.fields` so the omission receipt stays accurate. An explicit `--fields` stays authoritative."
